    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The database is persistently inaccessible (authentication error on every attempt — 8 retries including `SELECT 1` and `SHOW TABLES`), so data verification is impossible in this session. I will finalize based on the semantic-network evidence and the strong same-shape metric precedent (dw_3235), which matches the task's first four output columns exactly.\n\n---\n\n### 1. Entity Semantics\n\n**Tables**\n- **FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY**: Bridge table, one row per organization–DLC key assignment. Columns: `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY` (FK to FCLT_ORGANIZATION), `DLC_KEY` (e.g. 'D_AEROASTRO'). Used to filter organizations with a non-null DLC assignment before joining FCLT_ORGANIZATION.\n- **FCLT_ORGANIZATION**: Facilities organization dimension, one row per organization (levels 1–6). Carries `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`, `ORGANIZATION_NAME`, `DLC_KEY`, `DLC_NAME`. Parent of SPACE_UNIT.\n- **SPACE_UNIT**: Space unit dimension, one row per space-assignment unit. Carries `SPACE_UNIT_KEY`, `SPACE_UNIT_CODE`, `SPACE_UNIT` (name), `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`, `DLC_KEY`.\n- **MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY**: One row per DLC under 'Standard Hierarchy'; carries `DLC_KEY`, `DLC_NAME`, and 5-level path codes/names including `MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME` (e.g. 'Provost Area') and `MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_CODE`.\n- **SPACE_UNIT2**: Alternative space-unit lookup without `FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`; a strict subset of SPACE_UNIT (139 vs 150 rows per concept comparison).\n- **HR_ORG_UNIT**: HR organization unit dimension; carries HR hierarchy path and `ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME` ('Provost Area' variant); DLC_KEY joins may fan out.\n- **FAC_ORGANIZATION**: FAC_* family organization snapshot; keyed by `ORGANIZATION_KEY`, carries `D_CODE` not DLC_KEY/DLC_NAME; fewer organizations (169 vs 180).\n- **MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS**: DLC-to-administrative-object links (fund centers, facilities orgs, etc.).\n- **MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT**: Direct-parent department lookup only (no multi-level path).\n\n**Metrics (precedents)**\n- **dw_3235**: *Identical task shape* for the first four columns — \"For each department name and its corresponding facility organization key where the department is in the Provost Area, provide the number of organizations, the minimum department hierarchy level 3 code…\". Its SQL defines the `ProvostAreaDepts` CTE: `MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY m JOIN FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY f ON m.DLC_KEY = f.DLC_KEY WHERE m.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME = 'Provost Area' GROUP BY m.DLC_NAME, f.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY`.\n- **dw_1864**: Level-5 organizations + SPACE_UNIT counts joined via `FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY = SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY` — precedent for counting space units per organization through the DLC key.\n- **dw_3692**: Provost Area via HR_ORG_UNIT.ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME (alternative Provost-Area definition, HR-side).\n- **dw_2559**: Provost Area via `MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME = 'Provost Area'` — precedent for the master-hierarchy-side Provost filter.\n\n**Concepts**: concept_facility_organization_dimension (FCLT_ORGANIZATION vs FAC_ORGANIZATION), concept_space_unit_dimension (SPACE_UNIT vs SPACE_UNIT2), concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy (MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY vs HR_ORG_UNIT vs parent/links tables).\n\n**Column Concepts**: column_concept_dlc_key (universal cross-domain join key; unique per DLC in MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY, fan-out in HR_ORG_UNIT), column_concept_space_unit_key, column_concept_facility_organization_key (FCLT_* vs FAC_* key families must not be mixed).\n\n### 2. Lineage & Relationships\n- Join edges (from hints + column definitions): FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY ↔ FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY; FCLT_ORGANIZATION.DLC_KEY ↔ SPACE_UNIT.DLC_KEY; FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.DLC_KEY ↔ MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_KEY; SPACE_UNIT.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY ↔ FCLT_ORGANIZATION.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY.\n- dw_3235 lineage: MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY + FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY (+ HR_ORG_UNIT for its dispersion part). dw_1864 lineage: FCLT_ORGANIZATION + SPACE_UNIT + HR_ORG_UNIT. dw_2559 lineage: FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY + FCLT_ORGANIZATION + MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY + SPACE_UNIT.\n- Concept memberships: FCLT_ORGANIZATION ∈ concept_facility_organization_dimension; SPACE_UNIT ∈ concept_space_unit_dimension; MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY ∈ concept_dept_hr_org_hierarchy.\n\n### 3. Similar-Entity Differences\n\n**3a. Dimension matrix**\n| Dimension | MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY | HR_ORG_UNIT | FAC_ORGANIZATION | SPACE_UNIT | SPACE_UNIT2 |\n|---|---|---|---|---|---|\n| Granularity | 1 row/DLC (310) | 1 row/HR unit (641), DLC_KEY fan-out | 1 row/org (169) | 1 row/space unit (150) | 1 row/space unit (139, subset) |\n| Provost Area column | MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME (cited by dw_2559, dw_3235) | ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME (cited by dw_3692) | none | none | none |\n| Level-3 code | MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_CODE ✓ | HR_ORG_LEVEL3_NAME (name, not code) | ✗ | ✗ | ✗ |\n| Org attribution | via DLC_KEY | via DLC_KEY | ORGANIZATION_KEY/D_CODE | FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY ✓ | ✗ (concept comparison) |\n\n**3b. Task-Requirement Fitness**\n- Department name (DLC_NAME): MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY SUPPORTED (column def; dw_3235 precedent). HR_ORG_UNIT also has DLC_NAME but no level-3 *code* → NOT-SUPPORTED for that requirement.\n- Provost Area filter: MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME SUPPORTED (dw_3235, dw_2559 precedents; hint column mapping). HR_ORG_UNIT.ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME also SUPPORTED but lacks level-3 code.\n- Min/Max level-3 code: only MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_CODE SUPPORTED.\n- Organization key: FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY SUPPORTED (hint mapping; dw_3235). FAC_ORGANIZATION.ORGANIZATION_KEY VIOLATES key-family rule for SPACE_UNIT joins (column_concept_facility_organization_key).\n- Organization name: FCLT_ORGANIZATION.ORGANIZATION_NAME SUPPORTED; FAC_ORGANIZATION NOT-SUPPORTED (fewer rows, no DLC_KEY join to SPACE_UNIT).\n- Space unit count: SPACE_UNIT.SPACE_UNIT_KEY SUPPORTED (has org/DLC linkage); SPACE_UNIT2 NOT-SUPPORTED (no FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, subset coverage — concept decision_guide).\n\n**3c. Wording-to-Field Anchoring**: \"department name\" → MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY.DLC_NAME (hint mapping, dw_3235 precedent). \"Provost Area\" → MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_2_NAME = 'Provost Area' (hint + two metric precedents). \"organization key\" → FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY.FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY (hint). \"number of associated space units\" → COUNT(SPACE_UNIT.SPACE_UNIT_KEY) per organization name (hint subqueries 1/3). \"average number of space units\" → AVG of per-organization counts (hint subquery 3). \"LARGE/SMALL/AVERAGE_HOLDER\" → ±20% CASE thresholds (hint subquery 3). No ambiguity remains after hint anchoring.\n\n**3d. Precedent Usage Evidence**: Provost-Area-via-MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY + FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY org-count/min-level3 shape: 1 precedent (dw_3235) — exact match for columns 1–4. Space-unit-count-per-organization via DLC_KEY join: dw_1864, dw_2559 (2 precedents). HR-side Provost filter: dw_3692, dw_1864 (2 precedents) but neither produces level-3 codes.\n\n### 4. Business Usage\n- MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY: DLC scope filter and hierarchy-path reporting; consumed by dw_3235, dw_2559, dw_3692, dw_4776.\n- FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY: DLC-assignment filter bridge before FCLT_ORGANIZATION joins; consumed by dw_3235, dw_2559.\n- FCLT_ORGANIZATION: organization name/level/description reporting and space-unit parent; consumed by dw_1864, dw_3692, dw_2559, dw_4562.\n- SPACE_UNIT: space-unit counts per organization/DLC; consumed by dw_1864, dw_2559, dw_3916, dw_4330.\n- SPACE_UNIT2, FAC_ORGANIZATION, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS, MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT, HR_ORG_UNIT: related-domain tables; none supplies the level-3 code + org-key + space-unit combination required here.\n\n### 5. Coverage Checklist\nAll Phase 1 entities investigated: FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY, FCLT_ORGANIZATION, SPACE_UNIT, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY, SPACE_UNIT2, HR_ORG_UNIT, FAC_ORGANIZATION, MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY_LINKS, MASTER_DEPT_DCODE_PARENT (semantic_get); dw_3235, dw_1864, dw_3692, dw_2559 (semantic_get); 3 concepts + 3 column concepts (semantic_get). mysql_query attempted 8× — all failed with access-denied (infrastructure issue), so no data-level verification was possible.\n\n### 6. Recommendation\n\n**6a.** Use MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY (DLC_NAME, level-2 Provost filter, level-3 code min/max) + FCLT_ORG_DLC_KEY (FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY, org count) + FCLT_ORGANIZATION (ORGANIZATION_NAME) + SPACE_UNIT (SPACE_UNIT_KEY count via DLC_KEY).\n\n**6b.** Four CTEs following the hint decomposition and dw_3235 precedent: (1) `ProvostAreaDepts` = dw_3235's exact CTE; (2) join back to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY on DLC_NAME for MAX level-3 code (hint subquery 4); (3) `OrgSpaceUnits` = per-ORGANIZATION_NAME space-unit counts via fok→fo→su DLC_KEY joins (hint subqueries 1/3); (4) `AvgStats` = AVG of those counts, CROSS JOINed; CASE ±20% thresholds for holder category. Link the Provost rows to space-unit stats via FCLT_ORGANIZATION on FCLT_ORGANIZATION_KEY → ORGANIZATION_NAME. No ROUND anywhere (\"do not return rounded answers\"). Caveat: DLC_KEY joins can fan out (multiple orgs per DLC), but this is the exact pattern used by the hint decomposition and dw_1864/dw_2559 precedents.\n\n**6c.** *Data*: SPACE_UNIT is the only space-unit table with organization linkage and full coverage (150 vs 139 rows, concept comparison); MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY DLC_KEY is unique per DLC (no fan-out on the hierarchy side, column_concept_dlc_key). *Semantic-network*: dw_3235 is a verbatim precedent for columns 1–4; concept decision guides direct Provost/hierarchy questions to MASTER_DEPT_HIERARCHY and org-linked space-unit counts to SPACE_UNIT; key-family rule excludes FAC_ORGANIZATION. *Business*: the \"Provost Area department × facility organization key\" reporting pattern is established (dw_3235, dw_2559), and holder-category thresholding matches the hint's documented subquery 3.\n\n**6d.** Alternative: HR_ORG_UNIT.ORG_HIER_TOP_LEVEL_NAME = 'Provost Area' (dw_3692 style) — rejected because HR_ORG_UNIT has no MASTER_DEPT_HIER_LEVEL_3_CODE and its DLC_KEY joins fan out. No tie remains.\n\n",
      "tool_calls": [
